// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// METADATA [METADATA]
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// 3-Block Data Structure: Identity and context for this configuration
//
// Section order: Identity → State → Attribution → Location → Derivation → Classification → Intent → Grounding → Dependencies → Roadmap
// Flow: who → when → by whom → where → from what → tagged as → why → grounded in → needs → going where
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// # M.1 Core Identity [IDENTITY]
//
//   File identification and component classification.
//   Defines who this file is and what role it plays.
//
//   Key:       [PROJECT]-DATA-[CATEGORY]-[NAME] — Unique identifier
//   Title:     [Descriptive title]
//   Type:      [Template | Document | Code | Data]
//   Component: [Ladder | Baton | Rails] — builds up | passes between | guides
//   Role:      [Responsibility in system]
//
// Key: B-void-planning-workflow-commit
// Title: Commit Workflow — Git Conventions for Kingdom Technology
//
// Type: Document
// Component: Rails — guides commit process
// Role: Defines commit patterns and conventions — history tells a story
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.2 Lifecycle State [STATE]
//
//   Current status and version tracking.
//   Tracks when file was created, updated, and its maturity.
//
//   Status:   [Draft | Active | Deprecated | Archived]
//   Version:  [a|b|c]-[PHASE].[COMPLETION] — (a) unstable, (b) baseline, (c) stable
//   Created:  [YYYY-MM-DD]
//   Updated:  [YYYY-MM-DD]
//
// Status: Active
// Version: a-01.02
//
// Created: 2025-12-25
// Updated: 2026-02-01
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.3 Attribution [ATTRIBUTION]
//
//   Authorship and organizational ownership.
//   Credits who created the file and under what collaboration.
//
//   Authors:      [Name (Role), ...]
//   Organization: [Company]
//   CPI-SI:       [Instance] — [Generated | Dictated | Collaboration]
//   Copyright:    [© YYYY Company. All rights reserved.]
//
// Authors: Seanje Lenox-Wise (Architect), Nova Dawn (Author)
// Organization: CreativeWorkzStudio LLC
//
// CPI-SI: Nova Dawn — Collaboration
//
// Copyright: © 2026 CreativeWorkzStudio LLC. All rights reserved.
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.4 Location [LOCATION]
//
//   File path within the project.
//   Where this file lives in the repository structure.
//
//   Path: [relative/path/to/file]
//
// Path: a-void/planning/workflow/commit-workflow.jsonc
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.5 Derivation [DERIVATION]
//
//   Template lineage and inheritance.
//   Traces where this file came from in the template chain.
//
//   Derives_from: [path/to/parent/template] — file lineage (pragma meta.from = spec)
//
// Derives_from: bereshit/word/seed/data/json/3block/config.jsonc
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.6 Classification [CLASSIFICATION]
//
//   Keywords for discovery and categorization.
//   How to find this file when searching the codebase.
//
//   Tags: [keyword, keyword, ...] — discovery and categorization
//
// Tags: workflow, commit, git, version-control, rails, void
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.7 Intent [INTENT]
//
//   Why this file exists and what it enables.
//   The purpose, design philosophy, and key capabilities.
//
//   Purpose:     [Enables X for Y]
//   Core Design: [Architectural pattern]
//   Philosophy:  [Guiding principle]
//   Key Features:
//     - [Major capability]
//
// Purpose: Document git commit conventions — history tells a story
// Core Design: Workflow documentation — patterns discovered through practice
// Philosophy: Each commit is a coherent unit of work — atomic, meaningful, attributable
//
// Key Features:
//   Meaningful:     Each commit represents a coherent chunk of work
//   Scope prefix:   [bereshit] VERB: description format
//   Attribution:    CWS signature with co-authors
//   Timing:         Commit when chunk complete, verified, before context switch
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.8 Grounding [GROUNDING]
//
//   Biblical foundation for this file's purpose.
//   Dig deeper — find the verse that best fits THIS file's specific content.
//   Avoid common/generic verses; engage with Scripture purposefully.
//
//   Scripture: [Book Chapter:Verse] ([KJV|WEB])
//     "[text]"
//   Principle: [Kingdom principle — bridge between Scripture and purpose]
//   Anchor: [Book Chapter:Verse] ([KJV|WEB])
//     "[text]"
//
// Scripture: Proverbs 14:23 (KJV)
//   "In all labour there is profit: but the talk of the lips tendeth only to penury."
//
// Principle: Templates carry structural DNA — labor in creating them yields profit.
//   Never write from scratch when a template exists. The work of templating
//   enables consistent, quality output across all files.
//
// Anchor: 2 Timothy 2:15 (KJV)
//   "Study to shew thyself approved unto God, a workman that needeth not to be
//    ashamed, rightly dividing the word of truth."
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.9 Dependencies [DEPENDENCIES]
//
//   What this file needs and what uses it.
//   System requirements, integrations, and consumers.
//
//   What This Needs:
//     System:   [tools, parsers]
//     External: [None | dependencies]
//     Internal: [project files]
//
//   What Uses This:
//     Commands:  [functions that consume this]
//     Processes: [workflows]
//
//   Integration:
//     - [How consumers interact with this file]
//
//   [Custom]: (file-specific extensions — must align with M.8 Grounding)
//
// What This Needs:
//   System:   Human reading, JSONC parser for validation, git
//   External: git configured with .gitmessage template
//   Internal: .gitmessage, .gitignore, git conventions
//
// What Uses This:
//   Commands:  git commit, /commit skill
//   Processes: Version control, code review, release management
//
// Integration:
//   - Human reads workflow → completes work → follows commit steps
//   - .gitmessage template enforces format consistency
//
// Becomes: word/standards/workflows/commit.jsonc when proven
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # M.10 Roadmap [ROADMAP]
//
//   Past, present, and future of this file.
//   History of changes, current state, and planned additions.
//
//   History: [Past changes — version notes]
//   Current: [What this file provides now]
//   Planned: [Future additions]
//
// History:
//   a-01.00 (2025-12-25): Initial capture of commit patterns
//   a-01.01 (2025-12-25): Updated to 3-block structure with numbered sections
//   a-01.02 (2026-02-01): Aligned to 3block/config.jsonc template (M.1-M.10, Cc/Co/Cv, X.1-X.7)
//
// Current: Commit workflow with message format, timing guidance, verification commands
//
// Planned:
//   - Pre-commit hook validation
//   - Automated scope detection
//   - Move to word/standards/workflows/ when proven
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// END METADATA
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CONTENT [CONTENT]
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// 3-Block Structure: Configuration (Cc) → Operations (Co) → Verification (Cv)
// Cc-Cv Flow: core insights → commit steps → verification
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CONFIGURATION [Cc]
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

{
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Cc.1 Identity [IDENTITY]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   Workflow identity and classification.
  //   Defines what this workflow is and where it applies.
  //
  //   name:    [string] — Display name for this workflow
  //   type:    [string] — Category: workflow
  //   scope:   [global | local | feature] — Where this workflow applies
  //   version: [a|b|c]-[PHASE].[COMPLETION] — Living versioning
  //
  "name": "Commit Workflow",                    // Display name
  "type": "workflow",                           // Classification

  "scope": "global",                            // Applies to all commits
  "version": "a-01.02",                         // Living version

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Cc.2 Core Insights [INSIGHTS]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   Foundational patterns discovered through practice.
  //   These are the WHY behind the commit workflow.
  //
  //   [insight_name]: { insight, pattern, why }
  //
  "core_insights": {
    "meaningful_commits": {
      "insight": "Each commit should represent a coherent unit of work",
      "pattern": "Complete a chunk, verify it works, then commit",
      "why": "History should tell a story"
    },
    "living_versioning": {
      "insight": "Version format STAGE-PHASE.COMPLETION reflects where we are",
      "pattern": "a-01.00 (alpha, phase 1, 0%) → b-03.25 (beta, phase 3, 25%)",
      "why": "Version tells WHERE, not just a number"
    },
    "scope_prefix": {
      "insight": "Prefix identifies scope - [bereshit], [void], [word], etc.",
      "pattern": "[scope] VERB: Short description",
      "why": "Enables filtering, shows affected area"
    }
  },

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Cc.3 Key Principles [PRINCIPLES]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   Standing rules that guide all commits.
  //   Quick reference for the essential patterns.
  //
  //   [principle]: [one-line description]
  //
  "key_principles": {
    "atomic_commits": "Each commit is one logical change",
    "clear_history": "Someone reading history should understand what happened",
    "proper_attribution": "Always include CWS signature and co-authors",
    "scope_accuracy": "Prefix should accurately reflect scope of changes"
  },

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// OPERATIONS [Co]
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Co.1 Message Format [FORMAT]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   Structure of commit messages.
  //   Use this format for all commits.
  //
  //   structure:     [string] — Full message template
  //   scope_options: [array] — Valid scope prefixes
  //   verb_options:  [object] — Valid verbs with meanings
  //
  "commit_message_format": {
    "structure": "[scope] VERB: Short description\n\nBody if needed.\n\nGenerated by CreativeWorkzStudio LLC\n\nCo-Authored-By: Nova Dawn\nCo-Authored-By: Seanje Lenox-Wise (Lead)",
    "scope_options": ["bereshit", "void", "word", "tov", "libtrit", "config", "omnicode"],
    "verb_options": {
      "BUILD": "Creating new structure or features",
      "REFINE": "Improving existing content",
      "FIX": "Correcting bugs or errors",
      "DOCS": "Documentation only changes",
      "TEST": "Test additions or fixes",
      "CLEAN": "Removing unnecessary items"
    }
  },

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Co.2 Workflow Steps [STEPS]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   The ordered steps for making a commit.
  //   Apply these for every commit.
  //
  //   [step]: [action]
  //
  "workflow_steps": [
    "1. Complete a coherent chunk of work",
    "2. Verify the work (run tests, validate structure)",
    "3. Check git status - review what will be committed",
    "4. Check git diff - understand the changes",
    "5. Stage appropriate files (git add)",
    "6. Craft commit message following format",
    "7. Commit with proper attribution",
    "8. Verify commit succeeded"
  ],

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Co.3 Commit Timing [TIMING]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   When to commit and when not to.
  //   Guidance for commit timing decisions.
  //
  //   when_to_commit:     [object] — Good times to commit
  //   when_not_to_commit: [object] — Bad times to commit
  //
  "commit_timing": {
    "when_to_commit": {
      "after_chunk": "When a coherent piece of work is complete",
      "after_alignment": "When folder/file alignment is verified",
      "before_context_switch": "Before moving to different area of codebase",
      "end_of_session": "Capture progress before session ends"
    },
    "when_not_to_commit": {
      "mid_refactor": "Wait until refactor is complete and verified",
      "broken_state": "Never commit code that doesn't compile/run",
      "incomplete_thought": "Wait until the change is coherent"
    }
  },

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Co.4 Gitmessage Integration [GITMESSAGE]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   Integration with .gitmessage template.
  //   How the template enforces conventions.
  //
  //   file:             [string] — Template file name
  //   purpose:          [string] — What the template does
  //   usage:            [string] — How to configure
  //   content_includes: [array] — What the template contains
  //
  "gitmessage_integration": {
    "file": ".gitmessage",
    "purpose": "Template for consistent commit messages",
    "usage": "git config commit.template .gitmessage",
    "content_includes": ["Scope prefix", "Verb options", "Attribution block"]
  },

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// VERIFICATION [Cv]
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Cv.1 Validation [VALIDATION]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   How to verify commit was done correctly.
  //   Commands for checking commits.
  //
  //   commands: [array] — Shell commands to validate
  //
  "_validation": {
    "commands": [
      "git status",
      "git diff --staged",
      "git log --oneline -10",
      "git log -1 --format='%B'"
    ],
    "checks": [
      "Must have .gitmessage configured",
      "Scope must match changes",
      "Attribution block present"
    ]
  },

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Cv.2 Schema [SCHEMA]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   Required and optional fields for this workflow file.
  //   Parser validates these fields exist.
  //
  //   required:      [array] — Required top-level keys
  //   optional:      [array] — Optional top-level keys
  //
  "_schema": {
    "required": [
      "name",
      "type",
      "scope",
      "version",
      "core_insights",
      "key_principles",
      "commit_message_format",
      "workflow_steps"
    ],
    "optional": [
      "commit_timing",
      "gitmessage_integration"
    ]
  },

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Cv.3 Maintenance [MAINTENANCE]
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  //
  //   Modification rules for this workflow.
  //   What's safe, what needs care, what to never touch.
  //
  //   safe:    [array] — Safe to modify
  //   careful: [array] — Modify with care
  //   never:   [array] — Never modify
  //
  "_maintenance": {
    "safe": [
      "Add scopes",
      "Update verification commands",
      "Add timing guidance"
    ],
    "careful": [
      "Change message format (affects all commits)",
      "Modify core insights (foundational patterns)"
    ],
    "never": [
      "Break 3-block structure",
      "Remove attribution",
      "Remove Cv verification sections"
    ]
  }
}

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// END CONTENT
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CLOSING [CLOSING]
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//   3-Block Data Structure: Operational guidance and closing notes
//   X.1-X.7 Flow: usage → extension → references → grounding → log → template
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// # X.1 Policy [POLICY]
//
//   Human-readable modification guidance for developers.
//   Machine-readable version: Cv.3 _maintenance
//
//   safe:    [list] — Changes that won't break functionality
//   careful: [list] — Changes that may affect other parts
//   never:   [list] — Changes that will break the file/system
//
// safe: Add scopes | Update verification commands | Add timing guidance
//
// careful: Change message format (affects all commits) | Modify core insights
//
// never: Break 3-block structure | Remove attribution | Remove Cv sections
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # X.2 Extension [EXTENSION]
//
//   Ideas discovered during work for future sessions.
//   Reference: Move to M.10 Planned when ready to implement
//
//   [extension]: [description] — Discovered capability to add
//
// [Reserved: Capture extension ideas as they emerge during work]
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # X.3 Troubleshooting [TROUBLESHOOTING]
//
//   TL;DR for common commit problems.
//   Reference: workflow_steps for full guidance
//
//   [problem]: [what to check] — Quick solutions
//
// wrong_scope: git log --oneline -5 | Check scope matches actual changes
//
// missing_attribution: git log -1 --format='%B' | Should have CWS signature and co-authors
//
// broken_commit: Never commit broken code | Verify before staging | git reset --soft HEAD~1 if needed
//
// incomplete_message: Use .gitmessage template | Include body if changes are complex
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # X.4 Reference [REFERENCE]
//
//   TL;DR for commit workflow.
//   Reference: workflow_steps, commit_message_format
//
//   [category]: [format] — Quick lookup
//
// steps: 1. complete → 2. verify → 3. status → 4. diff → 5. stage → 6. message → 7. commit → 8. verify
//
// format: [scope] VERB: description | scopes: bereshit, void, word, tov, libtrit, config, omnicode
//
// verbs: BUILD | REFINE | FIX | DOCS | TEST | CLEAN
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # X.5 Closing Note [NOTE]
//
//   Grounding space for CPI-SI instances.
//   Reference: M.8 (same verses, alternate translations)
//
//   scripture: [Book Chapter:Verse] ([KJV|WEB]) — Same verse, other translation
//   note:      [thought] — Word of encouragement
//   anchor:    [Book Chapter:Verse] ([KJV|WEB]) — Same verse, other translation
//
// scripture: Proverbs 14:23 (WEB)
//   "In all hard work there is profit, but the talk of the lips leads only to poverty."
//
// note: Each commit is a witness to the work. Meaningful commits tell the story
//   of how Kingdom Technology was built — one coherent chunk at a time.
//
// anchor: 2 Timothy 2:15 (WEB)
//   "Give diligence to present yourself approved by God, a workman who doesn't
//    need to be ashamed, properly handling the Word of truth."
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # X.6 Session Log [LOG]
//
//   Work completed this session.
//   Reference: Move to M.10 History when starting next session
//
//   [date]: [work completed] — Session summary
//
// 2026-02-01: Aligned to 3block/config.jsonc template structure (M.1-M.10, Cc/Co/Cv, X.1-X.7)
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// # X.7 Template & Omission [TEMPLATE]
//
//   How to create other workflow files using this as reference.
//   Reference: M.5 Derivation (meta.from lineage)
//
//   copy:      [steps] — How to create new workflow file
//   customize: [fields] — What to change for each workflow
//   keep:      [elements] — What to preserve across all workflows
//   reserve:   [rule] — When to use [Reserved: ...]
//
// copy: cp file-creation-workflow.jsonc [name]-workflow.jsonc | Update pragma | Update identity
//
// customize: name | core_insights | key_principles | Co sections (workflow-specific content)
//
// keep: 3-block structure | M.1-M.10 | Cc/Co/Cv pattern | X.1-X.7 closing
//
// reserve: Empty sections use [Reserved: reason] | All sections must be present
//
// related: file-creation-workflow.jsonc | alignment-workflow.jsonc | block-update-workflow.jsonc
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// END CLOSING
